1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,520
The first real data set I have worked with professionally was a mess.

2
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:08,560
Not academic mess, real mess.

3
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:14,320
Column names with trailing spaces, dates formatted three different ways in the same column,

4
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:25,720
rows where someone had typed N-A, N-A, N-N-N, so something like this, so three different

5
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:33,400
kind of null values and a literal dash as four separate attempts at missing data.

6
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:39,640
Revenue figures mixed with strings like approximate, so I spent two weeks on that data set

7
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:46,200
before a nano single analysis, two weeks of Python loops that felt like archaeology.

8
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:46,200
Chipping away, never sure if you had found the actual data or just another layer of sediment.
